# TrizenDialog Frontend Resilience

**Scope:** `trizendialog-frontend/` only.

## Rule zero

Pages must continue functioning when one API request fails.

A failed widget must not crash or blank the page.

Prefer graceful degradation over hard failure.

```text
Dashboard
 ├ Messages Card ❌  → InlineError, rest of page works
 ├ Events Card ✅
 └ Activity Feed ✅
```

## Four states per data widget

Every data widget must handle:

```text
Loading → Skeleton
Error   → QueryErrorPanel or InlineError
Empty   → EmptyState (actionable when possible)
Success → Content
```

## Forbidden

```tsx
if (isError) {
  return <ErrorPage />;
}
```

on dashboard/list pages.

## Forbidden — API failure as empty

```text
isError === true && data === undefined → "No templates found"
```

That is misinformation. Check `isError` before treating missing data as empty.

## Required pattern

```tsx
if (isLoading) return <TableSkeleton />;

if (isError) {
  return (
    <QueryErrorPanel
      error={error}
      onRetry={() => void refetch()}
    />
  );
}

if (!data?.items.length) {
  return (
    <EmptyState
      title="No templates yet"
      description="Sync templates from your connected WhatsApp account."
      action={...}
    />
  );
}

return <TemplatesTable items={data.items} />;
```

Use shared components from `src/components/shared/`.

## Progressive rendering

Independent queries on one page must render independently. Do not block the whole page waiting for all queries.

## Error boundaries

Route-level `RouteErrorBoundary` is required. Unexpected render failures must not crash the entire application.

## Observability

`QueryErrorPanel` and mutation toasts use `getApiErrorMessage()`. When backend exposes `errorCode` or `correlationId`, surface them for support debugging.

Entity detail views should show `correlationId` when present on the DTO.
